    "prompt": "Below is a description of the Python function `format_stdin_to_stdout`.\n\nDescription:\n\"\"\"\nThe `format_stdin_to_stdout` function formats the content of standard input (stdin) according to the Black code formatter's rules and writes the formatted content to standard output (stdout). It accepts several parameters: `fast` determines whether to use a faster formatting mode, `content` allows providing the content directly instead of reading from stdin, `write_back` specifies how to handle the output (e.g., writing directly, showing a diff), `mode` defines the formatting style, and `lines` specifies which lines to format. The function returns `True` if the content was changed and `False` if it was not. It relies on helper functions like `decode_bytes`, `format_file_contents`, `diff`, and `color_diff`. If an exception of type `NothingChanged` is raised, the function returns `False` immediately. The function also handles edge cases such as ensuring a newline at the end of the output when `write_back` is `WriteBack.YES`. It has side effects by reading from and writing to stdin and stdout, respectively.\n\"\"\"\n\nSplit the description into atomic claims. Each claim must be a single, self-contained factual statement about the function that could be checked against the function's source code (name the function explicitly; no pronouns referring to other claims). Do not add claims that are not in the description; do not merge two facts into one claim. Keep the original wording where possible. Assign each claim exactly one type:\n- \"structural\": the function's signature, parameter names/defaults/types, return type, or which functions, methods, classes or attributes it uses.\n- \"dataflow\": how a value is computed, transformed, passed on, or what is returned for which input.\n- \"behavioural\": exceptions raised or caught, conditions/early returns, side effects, edge-case handling, ordering/iteration behaviour.\n- \"intent\": purpose, rationale, or the role of the function in the larger system.\n\nReturn a JSON array of at most 12 objects: [{\"text\": \"...\", \"type\": \"structural|dataflow|behavioural|intent\"}, ...]",
